Subject: [PATCH 053/154] feat: the General pane reads its values from the Rust
 core
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The running browser had NO settings reader after the Swift cut -
atrium_core_query appeared only in a unit test. atrium_settings_source adds
one: a path helper honouring ATRIUM_SETTINGS_FILE, which vm-scenario.sh
already stages, and a read that returns the core's loaded settings as JSON.

Nine rows, the lab's set and order. Five carry a key into the store; four have
no backend and render a dash rather than an empty cell, so a missing backend
looks different from a setting that is off.

TWO MISTAKES WORTH RECORDING, both mine, both caught by looking at the result
rather than the assertions.

The first read ran on the UI thread. That aborts the browser: 'Function marked
as blocking was called from a scope that disallows blocking'. I had written a
comment arguing for it. The read is on the thread pool now, and the comment
says why it has to be.

Then the push landed - 384 bytes, assertion green - and every row still showed
a dash. setSettings looked the root up as getElementById('root'); the host
page's root is 'atrium-root', so it found nothing and skipped every repaint in
silence. It holds the element installSettings was given now. The stylesheet had
the same wrong selector, which is why the rail sat above the body instead of
beside it.

13 DOM tests, up from 8, including one that fails if the repaint is skipped.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
